  "description": "The existing temporary storage containers within the upper yard are to be replaced with a timber-framed and clad, open-fronted carpenter's workshop, with a polycarbonate roof, on a new concrete base.\nThe existing brick partitions within the lower yard are to be replaced with a green barn, with two open fronted partitions and five closed partitions with roller shutters. This new partially insulated structure will be steel-framed and clad with steel sheeting - on a new concrete base. A solar array is to be included to the roof of the green barn, and provision will be made for rainwater collection.\nThe existing timber shed to the lower yard will be replaced with a new modular training room with the same footprint, on a new concrete base. This building is to feature redwood timber cladding and UPVC double-glazed windows.\nThe fence and gate to the southern boundary of the garden to Oak Lodge will be relocated further north to allow for a new vehicular entry, turning circle, and path to the residence.\nA new green oak fence will be erected to a section of the upper yard's perimeter, with access gates to either end.\nA new permeable concrete base hardstanding will be installed to the north east part of the upper yard.\nTo the north east section of the upper yard, provision will be made for a new vehicle wash station and new concrete battered wall panels to create partitions for materials storage.",
